summary: The content changes a stamp cannot see, outside files whose hash is kept fresh.

!! Content a stamp cannot see

A side's content counts as changed when its size, mtime, kind or link target did
([[Change detection in sync]]). A rewrite of the same size within the same mtime is
missed, as by the watcher — unless the file is marked <<cmd "mf_hash">> and the
watcher saw the rewrite: its hash is then read again ([[Content hashes kept fresh]]).
What remains open is the rest: a file not marked, or changed while nothing watched
it. Hashing every changed file on both sides would close it, at the cost the
planner avoids by comparing bytes only when a stamp moved.

The matching of records without a position, or moved before their first sync, is
settled: [[Why records are matched only by position]].
